{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Words and music by Pat Songwriter","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Typically this type of credit is aligned to the right, so that the position information refers to the right-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most part of the text. But in this example, the text is center-justified, not right-justified.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The halign attribute is used in these situations. If it is not present, its value is the same as for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"justify attribute. For elements where a justify attribute is not allowed, the default is implementation-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dependent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"halign","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection\/halign"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","title":"halign","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLOtherDirectionV6halignAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection\/halign"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftCenterRight":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"}],"title":"MXLLeftCenterRight","abstract":[{"text":"The left-center-right type is used to define horizontal alignment and text justification.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftcenterright","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherDirection/halign":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"halign","abstract":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection\/halign","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection\/halign","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherDirection":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOtherDirection"}],"title":"MXLOtherDirection","abstract":[{"text":"The other-direction type is used to define any direction symbols not yet in the MusicXML format. The smufl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute can be used to specify a particular direction symbol, allowing application interoperability without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-direction type without the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherDirection","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlotherdirection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOtherDirection"}],"type":"topic"}}}